diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index fa8aa2e..074fc15 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,22 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+### Added
+
+- `Validation::{External, Skip}` and `translate_sanitized_native_reflected_unvalidated`: the reflected
+  carrier with the external `spirv-val` gate skipped, for callers that cannot start a process. The two
+  structural rejects that follow the validator (`reject_function_constant_erased_effects`,
+  `reject_imageblock_only_effects`) still run. The command-line tool keeps `External`; its output is
+  byte-identical to the previous commit over a 1539-module corpus.
+- Workspace crate `n48xlate` (cdylib, LGPL-3.0-or-later): a C ABI (`n48x_abi_version`, `n48x_translate`,
+  `n48x_free`) that turns AIR text into SPIR-V plus the trimmed reflection, in process, for the Navi48
+  Metal bundle.
+- `n48xlate` ABI 2: `n48x_translate_linked` resolves an entry's direct visible-function references
+  (`.MTL_VISIBLE_FN_REF`) to the exact authored dependencies the caller passes (each sanitised like the
+  entry, only those the entry reaches transitively are used, a reference nobody authored is refused by
+  name) through `specialize_linked_module` before the unvalidated reflected translation. `n48x_translate`
+  is unchanged (an entry that names a visible function is still refused).
+
 ### Fixed
 
 - A texture argument the pipeline variant does not provide is no longer answered by the module's
